Billing rules (documented precedence):

1. Per-entry rounding: every time entry is rounded UP to the next 6-minute
   increment (0.1 h). 3h07m = 187 min -> 192 min -> 3.2 billed hours.
2. Daily overtime: hours beyond 8 in a single day bill at 1.25x. Within a
   day, entries fill the regular bucket chronologically first; hours past
   the 8h threshold (on whichever entry crosses it) are daily OT.
3. Weekly overtime: hours beyond 40 regular-equivalent hours per week bill
   at 1.5x, applied AFTER daily OT such that an hour is never double-counted.
   PRECEDENCE: weekly OT applies only to hours that were NOT already counted
   as daily OT -- i.e. we sum each day's sub-8h "regular candidate" hours;
   if that sum exceeds 40, the excess becomes weekly OT and is taken out of
   the regular pool (latest entries of the week first), never out of the
   daily-OT pool.

All money math uses Decimal. Invoice totals are quantized to cents
(ROUND_HALF_UP).
